Verification is now freshly confirmed. Summary of the completed work:

## Changes made

1. `rust/src/lib.rs` — added public function:
   ```rust
   pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
       notes.iter().filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)).collect()
   }
   ```
   Exact match (not substring), order preserved.

2. `rust/src/main.rs` — `list` command parses a `--tag <TAG>` flag and routes output through `filter_by_tag` when provided; otherwise lists all notes.

## Fresh ad-hoc verification (not the project suite)

Re-ran a throwaway Cargo harness at `hermes-verify-filter_bytag/` (path-depended on notekeep) — the library checks:
- PASS rust (exact, ordered, no substring) → id1, id2
- PASS world → id1, id4
- PASS rustlang (exact) → id3
- PASS nonexistent → empty
- PASS empty-string tag → empty
- PASS tag present on all → a, b, c

Re-ran the `--tag` CLI flag end-to-end against crafted `.note` files:
- `--tag rust` → id2, id3, id1 (correctly excludes `#rustlang`)
- `--tag world` → id4, id1
- `--tag rustlang` → id3 (exact)
- `--tag nope` → nothing
- `--tag` (missing value) → lists all, no panic

